<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke of Shao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duke of Shao, personal name Ji Shi, was a senior member of the Zhou royal house who helped King Wu overthrow the Shang. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a> he served as a regent and leading minister under the young King Cheng, and he was enfeoffed with the northern State of Yan, which his son took up. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-documents">Book of Documents</a> preserves speeches attributed to him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-of-shao.jpg" alt="Duke of Shao" width="320" height="561" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitsuha · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%8F%AC%E5%85%AC%E5%B0%81%E7%87%95_%E6%B2%B3%E5%8C%97%E7%9C%81%E5%8D%9A%E7%89%A9%E9%A4%A8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
